{
  "_README": "LIVE conformance vectors for the Canton V2 hash recompute. While preparedTx and topology are EMPTY, the conformance test marks its assertions pending (it.skip) so the green-gate stays green. As soon as a vector is added here it MUST pass \u2014 a present-but-mismatching vector FAILS the build loudly. Capture vectors with PREPARE/GENERATE-only calls (side-effect-free; they do NOT execute, finalize, or move money). See canton-hash.conformance.test.ts and the spec section C for the exact request/response shapes.",
  "_howToCapture": {
    "preparedTx": "POST /v1/wallet/submit/prepare (gated by enableAgentWallet; header X-Agent-Key if agentWalletApiKey set). Build the body via the resolve endpoints (POST /v1/wallet/resolve/transfer-factory for cip56, or /v1/wallet/resolve/transfer-command for v1) then assemble the exercise as packages/agent-wallet/src/tx.ts does. Save response.preparedTransaction -> preparedTransaction and response.hash -> hash. STOP after capture; do NOT call /v1/wallet/submit/execute.",
    "topology": "POST /v1/wallet/onboard/prepare with {publicKey:{format:CRYPTO_KEY_FORMAT_DER_X509_SUBJECT_PUBLIC_KEY_INFO, keyData:<SPKI DER base64 of the agent Ed25519 public key>, keySpec:SIGNING_KEY_SPEC_EC_CURVE25519}, partyHint:'agent'}. Save response.onboardingTransactions -> onboardingTransactions, response.hashToSign -> hashToSign, the EXACT publicKey.keyData you sent -> publicKeyKeyData, and response.publicKeyFingerprint -> publicKeyFingerprint. Prepare-only is side-effect-free; do NOT call /v1/wallet/onboard/finalize."
  },
